  "description": "Test 26 (PL3; hand-derived). The current producer is non-null only between the producer seed of state 3 and the end of state 4, and state 3 never sees it set (6.2: every writer of state 3 nulls it in the same call), so FreeCity4 always seeds [choice]. Pump of 1000 at (5,5) (water at (5,4), so capacity 1000, efficiency 1.0, production 1000), a house of 30 at (7,5). Four DoIdle calls (states 0, 1, 2, 3) leave state 4 pending with current = pump. A save then holds the pump's record in field 13 (offset 2 + 16 + 8 + 4096 + 4 + 4 + 8 + 4 + 4 + 40 = 4186): seed 5, 5, rectangle 5, 5, 5, 5, max capacity 1000, production 1000, then the occupant reference (4315 bytes in all). A copy has field 13 replaced by an all-zero record with a null reference (36 bytes, so 4311 in all). Loading the first sets current = pump (matched against the producer list) and state 0; loading the copy leaves it null. Either way the first pass after the load (Init, ConnectionsReady) clears it in state 2 and gives the same results: the network is the pump cell alone (no direction bits), the ring flood reaches the house at ring 2, consumed 30 <= 1000; published (7,5) = 3 (watered | lot), (5,5) = 7 (watered | lot | producer only); totals produced 1000, consumed 30; water used trunc(1000 x f32(30 / 1000)) = trunc(29.9999993 rounded to 24 bits = 30.0) = 30; history produced 1000, consumed 30, imported 0, exported 0, pipes 0, unused 0, watered 1, unwatered 0; pass counter 2.",
